<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35817" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕtītrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		id.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A female applicant</i> or <i>candidate</i> for office (post-Aug.), Auct. <i><span class="en">Quint.
				Decl. 252</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Judicial t. t., <i>a female claimant</i> or
				<i>plaintiff</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contra petitricem pronuntiavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					36, 1, 74 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
